      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <omp.h>\n#include <float.h>\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    long total = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) total += groups[i].length;\n\n    float *xs = malloc(total * sizeof(float));\n    float *ys = malloc(total * sizeof(float));\n    char *labs = malloc(total * sizeof(char));\n    long idx = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            xs[idx] = g.points[j].x;\n            ys[idx] = g.points[j].y;\n            labs[idx] = g.label;\n            idx++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    int nthreads = omp_get_max_threads();\n    float **tdist = malloc(nthreads * sizeof(float*));\n    char **tlab = malloc(nthreads * sizeof(char*));\n    for (int t = 0; t < nthreads; t++) {\n        tdist[t] = malloc(k * sizeof(float));\n        tlab[t] = malloc(k * sizeof(char));\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) tdist[t][i] = -1.0f;\n    }\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n        float *ldist = tdist[tid];\n        char *llab = tlab[tid];\n\n        #pragma omp for schedule(static) nowait\n        for (long i = 0; i < total; i++) {\n            float dx = xs[i] - to_evaluate.x;\n            float dy = ys[i] - to_evaluate.y;\n            float d = dx * dx + dy * dy;\n            char lab = labs[i];\n\n            int pos = -1;\n            for (int x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                if (ldist[x] == -1.0f || d < ldist[x]) { pos = x; break; }\n            }\n            if (pos != -1) {\n                for (int y = k - 1; y > pos; y--) {\n                    ldist[y] = ldist[y - 1];\n                    llab[y] = llab[y - 1];\n                }\n                ldist[pos] = d;\n                llab[pos] = lab;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    float *gdist = malloc(k * sizeof(float));\n    char *glab = malloc(k * sizeof(char));\n    int *ptr = calloc(nthreads, sizeof(int));\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) { gdist[i] = -1.0f; glab[i] = -1; }\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        int best_t = -1;\n        float best_d = FLT_MAX;\n        for (int t = 0; t < nthreads; t++) {\n            if (ptr[t] < k && tdist[t][ptr[t]] != -1.0f) {\n                float d = tdist[t][ptr[t]];\n                if (best_t == -1 || d < best_d || (d == best_d && t < best_t)) {\n                    best_d = d;\n                    best_t = t;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        if (best_t == -1) break;\n        gdist[i] = best_d;\n        glab[i] = tlab[best_t][ptr[best_t]];\n        ptr[best_t]++;\n    }\n\n    qsort(glab, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = glab[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (glab[i] != glab[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = glab[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = glab[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (int t = 0; t < nthreads; t++) { free(tdist[t]); free(tlab[t]); }\n    free(tdist); free(tlab);\n    free(xs); free(ys); free(labs);\n    free(gdist); free(glab); free(ptr);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Flatten all points into contiguous arrays and parallelize the distance/top-k loop with OpenMP static work sharing. Each thread maintains a private sorted top-k list using the same sentinel-based insertion as the sequential code; after an implicit barrier, deterministic merging of per-thread lists (tie-breaking by thread id, which corresponds to original point order under contiguous static scheduling) reproduces the exact global k nearest neighbors and preserves output bytes.",
  "notes": "Only src/knn.c is modified. The header remains unchanged. OpenMP pragmas are used for work sharing; no changes to input parsing or output format. Per-thread arrays avoid critical-section contention, and the merge step is O(k * nthreads).",
